WEBVTT

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:37.050
No way...

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:49.860
Someday, in this space deprived of hope,
kono takaki mubou no kuu de itsuka

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:54.530
you'll kneel of your own will.
sono ishi wa hiza wo tateru

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:05.750
break up foreordination

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:10.630
Was that flame an illusion or a friend?
fake ano hi wa nakama ka

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:15.380
Am I to venture into the darkness?
susumu beki wa yami ka

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:24.680
You'll find nameless emotions beyond the protruding knife.
knife tsukitateta saki ni shoutai no mienu kanjou

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:30.480
I can't let this end here yet.
ima wa mada koko de owarenai

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:35.650
I need to get ready to survive.
naraba ikiru junbi wo shiro yo

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:40.910
The passion in my heart only burns hotter.
uzu takaku tsumiageteku netsujou

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:44.450
Needless to say, it burdens me.
omotai ni kimatten darou

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:45.460
wake up your tough intention
Needless to say, it burdens me.
omotai ni kimatten darou

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:45.910
wake up your tough intention

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:46.830
Go ahead and mock my inexperience on the battlefield.
mijuku da to warau ga ii sa senjou
wake up your tough intention

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:51.090
mijuku da to warau ga ii sa senjou
Go ahead and mock my inexperience on the battlefield.

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:57.720
I'll show you what I've got, bit by bit,
hitotsu zutsu tashikamete yaru kara

00:01:58.180 --> 00:01:59.300
so bring it on.
kakattekoi

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:09.770
break up foreordination

00:02:14.990 --> 00:02:16.530
Run, Jamie!
Run, Jamie!

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:19.010
Come in! This is Command!

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:23.510
Somebody, come in!

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:24.200
Keep going.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:26.200
Someone, come in!

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:27.590
Someone...

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:31.610
This is Tanita!

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:34.750
Sergeant Tanita! What's the situation?

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:36.530
Enemy artillery!

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:38.530
Nothing around us yet...

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:41.640
How did this happen?

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:45.210
We were the only ones able to fire our flare,

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:47.020
so they targeted us.

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:49.980
That's what it'll say in the report.

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:52.870
Send a request to Battalion Commander Iriki to deploy.

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:55.760
Draw their attention away from us as much as you can.

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:56.720
Roger.

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:00.000
Is Jamie Hazaford there?

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.840
Captain! You're safe!

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:03.410
She's here.

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:06.180
Argevollen has shut down.

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:14.590
The pilot's alive,

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:16.340
but we can't even open the hatch,

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:18.690
let alone communicate with him.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:22.210
No...

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:28.830
The system routed all its power to pilot life support and shut down.

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:31.300
It's requesting a reboot.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:32.780
Can't you do it remotely?

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:34.770
No.

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:37.280
All I'm doing is reading its remote communications.

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:41.140
Someone must access Argevollen directly.

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:44.520
I must...

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:47.380
Captain.

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:51.310
What?

00:04:20.290 --> 00:04:21.280
I'm sorry.

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:23.970
This is all I have now.

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:30.630
You'll have to make it through the forest on foot to get to Argevollen.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:41.000
Good luck.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:47.600
Sorry I'm late!

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:53.240
I'll lead you to the front lines. Are you ready?

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:54.230
Y-Yes!

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:57.130
This way.

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:57.890
Right.

00:05:06.310 --> 00:05:09.030
That strange new model was taken out in a single hit?

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:11.720
It's not as good as the rumors say.

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:15.840
Colonel Iriki, Independent Attack Unit 8 is requesting our help.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:18.290
Oh, you survived, Samonji?

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:19.970
Tell them we'll leave immediately,

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:22.500
and to hold the front lines, at all costs, until we get there.

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:23.280
Yes, sir!

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:26.240
Even without that toy to draw the enemy's attention,

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:29.490
we still need them to function as a decoy, just like we planned.

00:05:32.090 --> 00:05:33.650
<i>That's impossible!</i>

00:05:33.650 --> 00:05:37.090
There's no way all of the other flares broke!

00:05:37.090 --> 00:05:39.630
Even so, there's nothing we can do about it.

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:41.190
But...

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:43.900
The enemy is focusing their fire on us.

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:45.520
What will we do?

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:47.450
Seeker.

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:50.200
The two of them are drawing the enemy's fire,

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:53.130
so at least the enemy's eyes aren't on us.

00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:53.700
However...

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:57.210
If the attack stops, we won't be able to stop the enemy's advance.

00:05:57.210 --> 00:06:01.350
That just means they can take full advantage of their long range guns.

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:02.500
Damn it!

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:04.510
Captain!

00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:08.190
Jamie Hazaford is on her way,

00:06:08.190 --> 00:06:12.180
and the cavalry battalion has already left.

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:17.760
I knew it! They used us as decoys!

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:18.750
Tanita.

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:19.540
Yes, sir.

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:21.900
How many flares do we have left?

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:22.610
Yamanami?

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:24.840
Two spares.

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:28.240
Use them to light the battalion's path.

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:30.860
Are you sure?

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:31.650
Go.

00:06:48.430 --> 00:06:51.300
I'm not even a soldier...

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:42.100
Talk about thrilling.

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:55.910
Ow...

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:10.590
Are you okay?

00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:16.700
I'm gonna demand workers' comp!

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:20.530
N-Nothing.

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:30.720
The battalion must be surprised.

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:34.320
We fired the spare flares our unit had.

00:08:34.870 --> 00:08:38.450
This time, we're having them buy time for us.

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:41.960
Time for us to reboot Argevollen, that is.

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:45.060
Which means that right now...

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:47.780
Everything's waiting on me?

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:51.970
I wish I hadn't heard that.

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:04.240
I never gave permission to launch flares!

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:08.360
Samonji, what are you thinking?

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:11.320
The 3rd Cavalry Battalion is engaged in combat.

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:13.320
It went well.

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:15.310
Stay on guard.

00:09:15.310 --> 00:09:18.110
Everyone, move your attack positions to the east.

00:09:18.110 --> 00:09:20.580
Don't let the enemy find Argevollen.

00:09:55.520 --> 00:09:57.820
Once we get through here, it's just a little further.

00:09:57.820 --> 00:09:59.090
Let's go.

00:10:06.930 --> 00:10:08.990
Let's hurry, Miss Hazaford.

00:10:12.810 --> 00:10:14.900
What if it doesn't work?

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:20.640
That wouldn't be surprising, would it?

00:10:21.670 --> 00:10:23.280
There's no way I can do this!

00:10:23.280 --> 00:10:26.640
I'm sorry, I can't handle this responsibility!

00:10:27.880 --> 00:10:28.850
<i>Now</i> you say it?

00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:43.780
Now's not the time to be saying that.

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:49.760
I-I'm sorry.

00:11:40.520 --> 00:11:41.680
Um...

00:11:42.620 --> 00:11:43.790
Um...

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:46.820
Answer me...

00:11:46.820 --> 00:11:48.690
What was your name?

00:11:50.280 --> 00:11:51.190
Hey!

00:11:51.190 --> 00:11:53.690
It's no good. There's no answer.

00:11:53.690 --> 00:11:55.010
Keep trying.

00:11:58.970 --> 00:12:00.520
What should I do?

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:17.000
Hello? Hello?

00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:19.350
Jamie?

00:12:20.060 --> 00:12:23.210
I'm so glad you're safe. Are you okay?

00:12:23.210 --> 00:12:25.180
Yeah, I guess I am.

00:12:25.180 --> 00:12:26.860
Where's Private Koshikawa?

00:12:27.510 --> 00:12:29.540
I don't see him anywhere.

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:31.250
Sorry.

00:12:34.760 --> 00:12:36.020
This is Koshikawa.

00:12:37.260 --> 00:12:38.020
Yes.

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:40.080
Yes.

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:45.920
Are you okay?

00:12:46.790 --> 00:12:48.370
What's going on up ahead?

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:50.550
The attacks are intensifying.

00:12:50.550 --> 00:12:53.820
This is the fastest way, but it'll be tough for someone without training.

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:57.090
Is there any other way?

00:12:57.090 --> 00:12:59.120
The safer, the better.

00:12:59.120 --> 00:13:00.910
It's a bit of a detour, but...

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:20.840
Damn it!

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:27.280
I can't do anything?

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:35.840
Am I going to die?

00:14:18.950 --> 00:14:19.840
Move.

00:14:33.920 --> 00:14:36.250
Argevollen device call.

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:38.600
Starting system boot-up sequence.

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:41.610
ID Number 06120530.

00:14:43.210 --> 00:14:46.610
Transcription: Jamie Hazaford. Active.

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:55.190
What are you doing? Go on.

00:15:05.770 --> 00:15:06.820
Hey!

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:29.990
Weapon expansions online.

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:32.780
Argevollen, all systems go!

00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:50.300
Yes! There it goes!

00:16:03.630 --> 00:16:04.690
Jamie.

00:16:18.220 --> 00:16:19.980
I see. Understood.

00:16:22.180 --> 00:16:24.960
Unit 8 will now begin its advance.

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:31.010
How much is left of the enemy cavalry?

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:34.450
We don't know anything about the ones who made it into our territory...

00:16:34.450 --> 00:16:36.720
Send the remaining Kriegers and soldiers.

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:38.700
Don't let anybody get through.

00:16:38.700 --> 00:16:39.490
Yes, sir.

00:16:45.130 --> 00:16:46.230
What's going on?

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:12.610
They destroyed the facility and withdrew before we got here?

00:17:38.460 --> 00:17:39.880
Good work.

00:17:39.880 --> 00:17:43.560
Go wash your face. You're wasting your beauty.

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:51.250
Thank you.

00:18:02.540 --> 00:18:03.280
Hey...

00:18:04.470 --> 00:18:05.480
What are you doing?

00:18:06.710 --> 00:18:10.260
I thought I might be able to learn something from the post-battle data,

00:18:10.780 --> 00:18:13.250
but I don't know how to view it.

00:18:14.110 --> 00:18:15.240
Move.

00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:31.210
When I was trapped inside Argevollen...

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:34.930
For the first time in my life I thought I might die.

00:18:37.450 --> 00:18:42.740
Actually, if you hadn't come, I would have.

00:18:49.510 --> 00:18:50.730
Thanks.

00:18:51.900 --> 00:18:57.000
I don't actually know anything about Trail Kriegers.

00:18:57.490 --> 00:19:01.060
Of course, I still have no interest in them at all,

00:19:01.060 --> 00:19:02.610
and I don't know if I ever will.

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:07.640
To be honest, I didn't care what company I worked for.

00:19:07.640 --> 00:19:12.720
I picked Kivernas Manufacturing because its pay was the best.

00:19:13.260 --> 00:19:14.680
That's all.

00:19:14.680 --> 00:19:16.260
I don't have anything.

00:19:16.900 --> 00:19:18.660
Any goals in life...

00:19:18.660 --> 00:19:21.120
Anything I want, anything I'm unhappy with...

00:19:21.690 --> 00:19:23.960
I've never wanted anything in life.

00:19:25.580 --> 00:19:28.140
However, something was missing.

00:19:31.560 --> 00:19:33.150
That's why...

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:40.910
That's why I get scared or angry at every little thing.

00:19:42.310 --> 00:19:47.620
It's all because I don't have any confidence in myself, right?

00:19:50.630 --> 00:19:51.540
But...

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:53.600
I can't talk like that now.

00:19:54.740 --> 00:19:57.630
I'm here now, aren't I?

00:19:59.120 --> 00:20:00.080
I see.

00:20:00.970 --> 00:20:01.630
Good luck.

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:07.260
Y-You, too.

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:08.130
Yeah.

00:20:14.340 --> 00:20:15.190
What?

00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:18.710
I didn't see that. Can you do that again?

00:20:18.710 --> 00:20:20.400
This is my job!

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:23.700
So this was the captain's answer?

00:20:25.120 --> 00:20:28.860
Instead of tying him down, let him do what he wants.

00:20:29.950 --> 00:20:34.170
Your next appointment has been decided.

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:39.090
You've just completed your mission, so I'm sure you want your troops to rest,

00:20:39.090 --> 00:20:40.050
but this is an order.

00:20:40.980 --> 00:20:42.580
I appreciate everything.

00:20:42.580 --> 00:20:43.430
Goodbye.

00:20:44.180 --> 00:20:46.310
The problems with the flares were an accident.

00:20:47.480 --> 00:20:50.770
They were all unusable, including the spares.

00:20:51.790 --> 00:20:56.190
It's unacceptable, but unpredictable things are commonplace on the battlefield.

00:20:56.940 --> 00:20:57.930
You understand that, right?

00:20:58.660 --> 00:20:59.370
Yes.

00:21:00.880 --> 00:21:02.440
I'm well aware.

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:09.450
Right, right...

00:21:10.470 --> 00:21:11.330
Mt. Suguro?

00:21:12.520 --> 00:21:14.450
Hello? This is Hazaford.

00:21:14.450 --> 00:21:17.710
This is Suguro. Thanks for your call earlier.

00:21:18.220 --> 00:21:22.650
I told the executives you'd accepted my offer.

00:21:22.650 --> 00:21:24.180
They were all very happy.

00:21:24.180 --> 00:21:27.720
Oh, you've been given a bonus.

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:29.470
Thank you.

00:21:29.470 --> 00:21:31.910
Well then, we're counting on you.

00:21:31.910 --> 00:21:33.460
Okay. Bye!

00:21:36.250 --> 00:21:38.210
A bonus?

00:21:45.380 --> 00:21:47.690
Young people are great.

00:21:47.690 --> 00:21:50.800
Give them a huge sum of money, and they're happy as clams.

00:21:50.800 --> 00:21:55.660
It also looks like we'll be getting the data we need sooner than expected.

00:21:55.660 --> 00:21:57.300
I see.

00:21:57.300 --> 00:21:58.760
That's good to hear.

00:23:33.970 --> 00:23:37.760
Verhuls
